      "text": "symmetric but not reflexive",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "9N8yJ",
      "text": "transitive but not reflexive",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "cpKMt",
      "text": "reflexive and symmetric but not transitive",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "For every real number $x, x^{2} \\geq 0$\r\n$\\therefore$ $(x, x) \\in P$\r\nHence, $P$ is reflexive.\r\nNow let $(x,y) \\in P \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow xy \\geq 0 \\\\\r\n\\Rightarrow yx \\geq 0$\r\n$(y, x) \\in P$\r\nHence, $P$ is symmetric. \r\nAgain (-1,0)$\\in P$ and (0,2)$\\in P$\r\nBut (-1,2)$\\notin P$\r\n$as(-1)(2)=-2    < 0$\r\nPis not transitive.",
    "image": null
  },
